cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "related-party-lending-network: the insider relationships behind Ghana's 2019 savings and loans failures"
message: "If you use this evidence base or the network built from it, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
version: 0.7.0
authors:
  - family-names: Baah
    given-names: Samuel Ato Kwame
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Accra, Ghana"
    email: samatohobbs@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8773-7525"
abstract: >-
  The insider relationships behind the savings and loans companies and finance houses whose
  licences the Bank of Ghana revoked on 16 August 2019, modelled as a network built only from
  primary sources: what two regulators published and one court judgment found. Every node and
  every edge carries a quoted passage and a line number in the source that supports it, and the
  loader refuses to build if a quotation is not verbatim at the line its citation names. Analyses
  that returned nothing are published alongside those that did.
keywords:
  - network analysis
  - related-party transactions
  - bank failure
  - corporate governance
  - regulatory data
  - Ghana banking sector clean-up
  - reproducible research
